From 2b52e8174c127a8c54ef877f21912b6a147f6ab2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 5 Jul 2026 15:49:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 16/39] media: rockchip: rga3: map scattered userptr through
 IOMMU

RGA3 command streams carry base addresses, not scatterlists. The
forward-port therefore rejected userptr sg-tables whenever dma_map_sg()
returned more than one DMA segment. Runtime diagnostics proved those
returned IOVAs can be scattered and even descend, so relaxing the check
would reintroduce the MMU fault.

Add a Route B fallback for driver-owned sg-tables. After a normal DMA map
fails the single-span contract, unmap it, clear the sg-table DMA
bookkeeping left by that abandoned map, allocate one IOVA range from the
DMA domain cookie, map a page-aligned copy of the sg-table with
iommu_map_sg(), and program the synthetic base plus the original page
offset. Fail closed if the IOVA granule is larger than PAGE_SIZE, where
padding could break RGA's byte-contiguous view. Keep dma-buf imports on the
fail-closed DMA API contract.

Expose the DMA-API IOVA allocator through a small iommu-dma helper instead
of casting the private cookie through an RGA shadow type. Also move the RGA
IOVA guard-band constant to the shared header, sync non-contiguous buffers
through the same device used for mapping, and mark writable userptr pages
dirty before dropping their GUP references. Harden the 32-bit span
validator so arithmetic overflow fails closed.

Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@example.invalid>
